  "notes": "⛔ **\"A deliberately un-trap drum layer under a trap 808\" is the entry, and it is authored as a kick that stops syncopating.** `anchors` is `[\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\"]` with `syncopation` 0.08 and `tresilloBias` 0 — the steady quarter pulse the research calls \"closer to house/club than trap\" — under an 808 that stays an 808. That pairing is what makes this legible against `travis-porter`, the batch's other four-on-the-floor lean, which sits 20 BPM faster with a genuinely syncopated remainder and a snap/cowbell layer this record has none of. The tempo band is the lowest here (120–132). The second identity is looseness: \"sung hook with conversational contour and unquantized pitch\" is `quantizeStrength` 0.78, the loosest in this batch, with `articulation: legato`, `densityPerBar` [2, 5] and an `emptyBarBias` that leaves the bar alone. The 808 is \"a sustained sub drone with slow glides, less percussive than the ATL norm\": `slideProb` 0.3 but only one or two slides per four bars, and `sustain: legato` over a narrow low register. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` — the research rates the record high-medium and its sourcing is retrospectives rather than a session account. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the pad-swell transition (authored as `dropOutBeats` rather than as a swell, which the arranger has no lane for), and the family weights.",
